From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matt Hargett <plaztiksyke@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 May 2026 19:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Port wasmz to Zig 0.16 stdlib + add static-lib target

wasmz is pinned to Zig 0.15.2 but Zig 0.15s build runner segfaults on
macOS 26 Tahoe (its bundled libSystem TBDs are missing _realpath$DARWIN_EXTSN,
_sigaction, etc.). This patch ports the wasmz sources to the 0.16 stdlib so
the codebase builds with the working 0.16 toolchain.

Mechanical migrations:

  * std.meta.intToEnum(E, x) catch ... → std.enums.fromInt(E, x) orelse ...
    (0.16 returns ?E instead of !E)
  * std.ArrayListUnmanaged(T){} → .empty / explicit type ascription
    (default init of the unmanaged variant is deprecated)
  * std.meta.TagPayload(U, tag) → @FieldType(U, name) builtin
  * std.posix.mprotect was removed — call std.c.mprotect directly.
  * std.posix.PROT.NONE / .READ / .WRITE no longer exist as plain enum
    constants on Apple targets (it's now vm_prot_t, a packed struct).
    Replace with literal packed-struct values.
  * std.Thread.Mutex / Condition moved to std.Io and require an Io
    parameter — stub locally; the only caller is the wasm-threads
    atomic.wait/notify path which is gated by single_threaded and is
    not exercised by App-Store-eligible (single-threaded) embedders.
  * std.time.nanoTimestamp was removed — call clock_gettime(MONOTONIC)
    directly (same paths as above).
  * Target.Os.Tag.solaris was merged into .illumos — drop the stale arm.
  * Add Apple targets (.ios/.tvos/.watchos/.visionos) to the mmap-strategy
    selector — they all support mmap/mprotect (verified).

New build artefact:

  * static-lib step that mirrors the existing clib step but emits
    libwasmz.a, used by wasm-benchmark to link wasmz into an
    iOS/watchOS/tvOS App-Store-eligible bundle.
---
diff --git a/build.zig b/build.zig
index 9768a4c..befb75a 100644
--- a/build.zig
+++ b/build.zig
@@ -285,6 +285,29 @@ pub fn build(b: *std.Build) void {
     clib_step.dependOn(&b.addInstallArtifact(clib, .{}).step);
     clib_step.dependOn(&install_header.step);
 
+    // Static-lib companion of `clib` — built so Apple Store-eligible iOS /
+    // watchOS / tvOS apps can link wasmz in directly (no JIT, no dlopen).
+    // Mirrors the wasm-benchmark project convention (`zwasm` exposes the
+    // same `static-lib` step) so `scripts/build-wasmz.sh` can call it
+    // without a special case.
+    const clib_static = b.addLibrary(.{
+        .name = "wasmz",
+        .linkage = .static,
+        .root_module = b.createModule(.{
+            .root_source_file = b.path("src/capi.zig"),
+            .target = target,
+            .optimize = optimize,
+            .imports = &.{
+                .{ .name = "wasmz", .module = mod },
+            },
+            .link_libc = true,
+        }),
+    });
+
+    const static_lib_step = b.step("static-lib", "Build the C static library (libwasmz.a)");
+    static_lib_step.dependOn(&b.addInstallArtifact(clib_static, .{}).step);
+    static_lib_step.dependOn(&install_header.step);
+
     // ── wasmz-as-WASI (self-hosted CLI) ─────────────────────────────────────
     //
     // Build with: zig build wasi
